---
description: Living docs — patch repeating anti-patterns same turn; lint when mechanical; do not wait to be asked
alwaysApply: true
---

# living-docs (always on)

Follow the installed **`living-docs`** skill (`.agents/skills/living-docs`) — procedure + **placement** table. Slash: `/living-docs` (formerly manage-docs).

When the user corrects copy/UX **or** the same *class* of mistake repeats **or** verify-work finds a gap **or** placing a new Cursor artifact:

1. **Same turn as the code fix** — patch the matching topic under `{{anti-patterns-dir}}` (index: `{{anti-patterns-index}}`). Verify gaps / new proof classes → acceptance/evidence table at `{{path-to-acceptance-evidence}}`. Architecture invariants → `{{agents-guide}}`. Architecture topology → `{{architecture-map}}`.
2. **Only if it will probably repeat.** Prefer strengthen/merge over add. Skip one-offs.
3. **Dedupe gate** — search siblings → merge prefer invent → `{{docs-dedupe-command}}` when available. Reply: strengthened vs added.
4. **Codify mechanical bans** in the project linter same turn when the ban will keep mattering; cite the rule on the anti-pattern line.
5. **Placement** — agents guide vs rule vs anti-pattern vs skill vs agent (see skill). Prefer extend over new file.
6. **Do not wait to be asked.** Anti-patterns only — no post-mortems.
